/**
 * @page architecture Operon architecture
 *
 * Operon has a narrow execution spine: a dataset and problem define a symbolic
 * regression task; algorithms evolve trees; evaluators score those trees; and
 * selection/reinsertion feed the resulting individuals back into the search.
 * This page is the map for the system-level documentation. It describes
 * responsibilities and boundaries, not every public symbol.
 *
 * @section architecture-map System map
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph operon_architecture {
 *   rankdir=LR;
 *   graph [pad=0.2, nodesep=0.5, ranksep=0.8];
 *   node [shape=box, style="rounded"];
 *   "Dataset / Problem" -> "Tree / Node / PrimitiveSet";
 *   "Parser / Formatter" -> "Tree / Node / PrimitiveSet";
 *   "Tree / Node / PrimitiveSet" -> "Interpreter / JIT";
 *   "Tree / Node / PrimitiveSet" -> "Interval / Affine bounds";
 *   "Interpreter / JIT" -> "Evaluators";
 *   "Interval / Affine bounds" -> "Shape constraints";
 *   "Evaluators" -> "Shape constraints";
 *   "Evaluators" -> "GP / NSGA-II";
 *   "Shape constraints" -> "GP / NSGA-II";
 *   "GP / NSGA-II" -> "Creators / generators / mutation / crossover";
 *   "GP / NSGA-II" -> "Selection / reinsertion / archive";
 *   "Optimizers" -> "Evaluators";
 *   "Algorithms / evaluators" -> "CLI / probes / serialization";
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 * @section architecture-systems System documentation sequence
 *
 * - @ref core_model — dataset and problem formulation, postfix trees, nodes,
 *   primitive generation vocabulary, and enumeration grammar.
 * - @ref execution — parser, dispatch, interpreter, JIT, automatic
 *   differentiation, interval/affine evaluation, and range tightening.
 * - @ref evaluation_shape_constraints — evaluator phases, scoring, shape
 *   certification, enforcement, cache lifetime, and the hard-reject path.
 * - @ref search_optimization — GP/NSGA-II generation flow, variation,
 *   selection, reinsertion, non-dominated sorting, archive, and evaluation
 *   budgets.
 * - @ref search_optimization — linear scaling, local search, likelihood
 *   objectives, and solver boundaries.
 * - @ref architecture_integration — CLI configuration, probes, formatting,
 *   serialization, custom primitives/evaluators, and Python bindings.
 *
 * Each system page must state its public entry points, owned and borrowed state,
 * invariants, failure model, hot-path cost, and the diagrams that explain control
 * or data flow. API reference belongs in Doxygen comments beside the symbols;
 * these pages explain how the APIs compose.
 *
 * @section architecture-core Core model
 *
 * @anchor architecture_core
 * @ref core_model documents the representation and formulation boundary.
 *
 * @section architecture-execution Execution and symbolic semantics
 *
 * @anchor architecture_execution
 * @ref execution documents sampled interpretation, derivatives, and bounds.
 *
 * @section architecture-search Evolutionary search
 *
 * @anchor architecture_search
 * To document next: population lifecycle, offspring generation, local search,
 * evaluation budgets, GP, NSGA-II, archive updates, selectors, and reinserters.
 *
 * @section architecture-optimization Coefficient optimization
 *
 * @anchor architecture_optimization
 * To document next: linear scaling, optimizer callbacks, likelihood evaluators,
 * solver error boundaries, and the relation between optimized coefficients and
 * an @c Individual genotype.
 *
 * @section architecture-integration Integration surface
 *
 * @anchor architecture_integration
 * To document next: command-line configuration, shape-constraint JSON,
 * serialization/formatting, probes, custom registries, and pyoperon-facing API.
 */
